    // step Implement {
    //     // mhl's declared `prompt Name(...) { "...${param}..." }` templates
    //     // (language-design.md sec 2) can't express this per-feature,
    //     // per-attempt text: resolvePromptArgument (prompt_ops.go) only
    //     // recognizes a template reference written literally as the
    //     // `prompt:` argument, and every one of ITS OWN arguments must
    //     // itself be a literal string token (ast.StringValue on the raw,
    //     // unevaluated AST) — never a runtime expression like
    //     // current.title. There is also no way to obtain a rendered
    //     // template's text outside that one special position (so it can't
    //     // be concatenated with dynamic data either), and `skill`
    //     // declarations aren't wired into agent.run at all — a repo-wide
